2.3 Functions
These materials can also include custom functions. This is a custom function to round up from .5, which is necessary as the default {round} function rounds to the nearest even digit according to IEC 60559.
These functions can be in blocks below, or as separate R scripts.

nround &lt;- function(values, digits) {
  factor &lt;- 10^digits
  is_neg &lt;- ifelse(values &lt; 0, -1, 1)
  result &lt;- is_neg*floor(abs(values)*factor+.5)/factor
  return(result)
}

2.4 Data Manipulation
Every good dataset needs some averages or sums, and we all need to recode a variable or two.

df &lt;- df |&gt;
    rowwise() |&gt;
    mutate(job_knowledge_total = sum(jk1,jk2,jk3)) |&gt;
    ungroup() |&gt;
    mutate(job_knowledge_quintile = ntile(job_knowledge_total,5))

df$sex_factor &lt;- df$male |&gt;
    recode( 
        `0` = "Female", 
        `1` = "Male"
        )
